SPW-002 undo manifest.reason:
The manifest has the same fields as Save-DesktopOrganizationManifest (RunId, CreatedAt, Computer, User, BaseDirectory, UndoneAt, Entries[Action, Source, Destination, Category, Reason, Time]) and is written only when records exist. Undo replays in reverse:
- move/displace: only when Destination is a file and Source is free;
- copy/link: moved to state/undone/<runId>, and a link is skipped while its folder is non-empty (the Windows rule);
- mkdir: rmdir only when empty, dotfiles included.
Nothing is overwritten. UndoneAt is replaced only when errors == 0; otherwise the failures are printed, the run stays open, and the default undo picks the same newest open run again. Replace and duplicate pairs restore in the correct order. Quoted patsub replacements are safe under bash 5.2 patsub_replacement.
